From f918dcfc7735477173f58e25d1bd4dd732312925 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:53:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix real bug: roblox_username was actually storing the
 display name

Roblox's OAuth userinfo response uses OIDC-standard claim names that don't
mean what they sound like: 'name' and 'nickname' are both the DISPLAY name;
the real unique @username is 'preferred_username'. roblox-oauth had name ->
roblox_username and nickname -> roblox_display_name, so every user's stored
username was actually their display name duplicated - the real username was
never captured. This is why display-name search worked and username search
never could: there was no real username anywhere to search.

- Fixed the field mapping in roblox-oauth for all future logins
- Added backfill-roblox-usernames, a one-time function that repairs every
  existing user's row via Roblox's public Users API (looks up the real
  username from their already-known roblox_user_id). Only touches rows where
  username currently equals display name (the bug's exact symptom). Safe to
  run more than once. Delete this function after running it once.

Also: bot's discord.js 'ready' event can hang forever with zero log output if
the Server Members privileged intent is requested but not actually enabled
in the Developer Portal - which reads as a crashed/hung Railway deploy
(exactly what was reported: empty logs, then Bad Gateway). Fixed:
- HTTP server now starts immediately, independent of Discord login, so
  Railway's health check has something to hit right away and /health stays
  reachable even while Discord is still connecting or has failed entirely
- Added a 30s timeout around the 'ready' wait so a stuck intent produces a
  clear, loud error naming the likely cause instead of hanging silently
- /health now reports discordConnected: true/false
- Routes that need Discord return a clear 503 instead of failing obscurely
  if hit during the brief window before login completes
- Added global uncaughtException/unhandledRejection logging so nothing dies
  silently again

